WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:14.595
He was one of the biggest movie stars in the 1990s.

2
00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:21.298
So why did he live in a small, dirty home that was polluted with his own waste?

3
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:31.784
He was also underweight and had terrible tooth and skin problems— not very attractive for a world-famous actor.

4
00:00:33.452 --> 00:00:37.555
But few people knew the sad truth about Keiko, the killer whale.

5
00:00:41.137 --> 00:00:45.440
Killer whales, also known as "orcas," are found in oceans around the world.

6
00:00:46.641 --> 00:00:49.743
Keiko was born in the Atlantic, off the coast of Iceland.

7
00:00:51.424 --> 00:00:56.608
At around age two, Keiko was captured by a crew aboard a fishing boat and taken to an

8
00:00:56.648 --> 00:01:02.552
aquarium. A few years later he was sold to a water park in Canada.

9
00:01:04.188 --> 00:01:07.189
There, Keiko began training to be a performer.

10
00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.530
Then he was sold to an amusement park in Mexico.

11
00:01:13.251 --> 00:01:18.132
For the next ten years, Keiko starred in over seven thousand performances at the park.

12
00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:23.314
He was hand-fed about sixty kilograms of dead fish each day.

13
00:01:26.575 --> 00:01:29.716
But his pool was too small, and Keiko was bored.

14
00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:34.035
His dorsal fin, located on his back, was droopy.

15
00:01:36.997 --> 00:01:41.861
This meant Keiko was spending too much time on the surface of the water and swimming in only

16
00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:42.702
one direction.

17
00:01:47.246 --> 00:01:58.315
However, most audiences were not aware of Keiko's poor living In 1993, when Keiko starred in the movie

18
00:01:58.415 --> 00:02:01.125
Free Willy, his life changed forever.

19
00:02:02.366 --> 00:02:05.768
Free Willy is about a boy and a water-park whale named Willy.

20
00:02:07.449 --> 00:02:13.052
The boy, who is deeply attached to Willy, finds out that Willy's owners are planning to kill the

21
00:02:13.092 --> 00:02:19.116
whale. The boy does everything he can to save, and eventually free, Willy.

22
00:02:22.258 --> 00:02:25.680
The movie was a big hit and touched audiences everywhere.

23
00:02:28.584 --> 00:02:33.949
It also led many people to think about Keiko's real-life situation.

24
00:02:34.089 --> 00:02:41.356
In 1994 the Free Willy-Keiko Foundation was established to rescue Keiko and release him back into the wild.

25
00:02:43.458 --> 00:02:47.562
Thousands of children from around the world also campaigned for Keiko's freedom.

26
00:02:51.465 --> 00:02:54.068
They wrote letters to politicians and raised money.

27
00:02:58.128 --> 00:03:03.071
At last the amusement park in Mexico agreed to donate Keiko to the foundation.

28
00:03:04.672 --> 00:03:07.333
The foundation planned to return Keiko to the wild.

29
00:03:08.494 --> 00:03:11.135
But first they had to teach him how to live there.

30
00:03:12.316 --> 00:03:15.118
They built a new home for Keiko in the United States.

31
00:03:16.518 --> 00:03:19.700
But how could they move a seven-thousand-pound killer whale?

32
00:03:21.421 --> 00:03:26.464
UPS, a package delivery service, volunteered to move Keiko to his new home.

33
00:03:29.088 --> 00:03:33.151
Keiko's new home in Oregon was a large, custom-made pool by the ocean.

34
00:03:34.792 --> 00:03:39.495
There, for the first time in many years, Keiko swam in natural seawater.

35
00:03:42.117 --> 00:03:46.120
Ten dedicated trainers helped Keiko learn how to live in the wild again.

36
00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:52.724
Killer whales in the wild often swim as much as 160 kilometers every day.

37
00:03:54.485 --> 00:03:58.328
Each day Keiko had to swim farther and faster than before.

38
00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.541
As he improved and grew stronger, the trainers encouraged and rewarded him.

39
00:04:08.642 --> 00:04:11.583
Keiko especially liked to get his back and fins rubbed.

40
00:04:13.603 --> 00:04:16.844
It was also important for Keiko to learn how to catch his own food.

41
00:04:19.085 --> 00:04:21.285
The trainers put live fish into the water.

42
00:04:22.085 --> 00:04:25.346
At first Keiko would catch a fish and then release it.

43
00:04:28.927 --> 00:04:31.988
He had to be taught to eat the live fish after he caught them!

44
00:04:33.612 --> 00:04:36.774
For about a year, Keiko learned how to live in the wild.

45
00:04:38.996 --> 00:04:41.618
He gained weight and his skin problems vanished.

46
00:04:43.179 --> 00:04:46.461
But best of all, his dorsal fin began to uncurl.

47
00:04:48.002 --> 00:04:50.404
That meant Keiko was doing just fine.

48
00:04:52.745 --> 00:04:55.047
Killer whales are very close to their families.

49
00:04:57.348 --> 00:05:02.352
The trainers thought Keiko should return to his birthplace, where he might reunite with his family.

50
00:05:04.092 --> 00:05:08.316
After two years in the U.S., Keiko was taken back to Iceland.

51
00:05:10.157 --> 00:05:13.840
For almost twenty years, Keiko had been dependent on humans.

52
00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.964
Now he would have to survive on his own in a natural environment.

53
00:05:20.345 --> 00:05:23.308
The trainers slowly helped Keiko adjust to his new home.

54
00:05:24.869 --> 00:05:29.452
They allowed Keiko to go into the sea for an hour or two and followed him in small

55
00:05:29.492 --> 00:05:33.496
boats. Then they would direct him back to a pen.

56
00:05:35.508 --> 00:05:38.570
They gradually increased the time Keiko spent in the ocean.

57
00:05:41.612 --> 00:05:45.074
Soon Keiko was behaving like a wild killer whale.

58
00:05:47.795 --> 00:05:50.297
He spent more time underwater than on the surface.

59
00:05:53.038 --> 00:05:55.400
He began competing with other animals for food.

60
00:05:57.441 --> 00:06:02.484
He even made contact with wild killer whales near his pen by calling out to them.

61
00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.341
The trainers continued to monitor his progress.

62
00:06:09.322 --> 00:06:13.144
At last, in 2002 Keiko was released.

63
00:06:15.424 --> 00:06:20.967
Strong and free, he swam about 1,400 kilometers to Norway's coast.

64
00:06:23.128 --> 00:06:29.030
Thanks to the hard work of caring people, Keiko finally got to live as a killer whale should.

65
00:06:31.771 --> 00:06:35.218
In December 2003 Keiko died of an illness.

66
00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:41.926
But the killer whale who brought warmth and joy to the hearts of millions around the world will

67
00:06:42.106 --> 00:06:43.508
always be remembered.
